IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lca-juveniles`
IMPORT `lca-qa`

-- Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA), juveniles -- cases for the Q&A layer (lca-qa.l4): every exported question, for every
-- role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the value under which the situation does not
-- hold (FALSE) and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a
-- BOOLEAN, so the trap of graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- For the young person (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the
-- text (most taken from the baseline's own cases, lca-cases-juveniles.l4; c025 is Chloe turning 18), and once against the
-- baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the adult and the licensee
-- or seller, the values are worked by hand from the text.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked place` IS A Place
ASSUME `an unasked companion` IS A Companion
ASSUME `an unasked reason` IS A Reason
ASSUME `an unasked supplier` IS A Supplier
ASSUME `an unasked seller role` IS A `Seller role`
ASSUME `an unasked document` IS AN Evidence
ASSUME `an unasked offence` IS A `My offence`
ASSUME `an unasked supplier position` IS A `Who I am to the young person`
ASSUME `an unasked relation` IS A `How I am related to the young person`
ASSUME `an unasked companion of theirs` IS A `Who is with the young person`
ASSUME `an unasked part` IS A `My part in the sale`
ASSUME `an unasked part in the presence` IS A `My part in the young person's presence`
ASSUME `an unasked adult offence` IS AN `Adult offence`
ASSUME `an unasked business offence` IS A `Business offence`

`as the young person` MEANS `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)`
`as the adult` MEANS `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person`
`as the licensee or seller` MEANS `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor`

§§ `For the young person (the baseline's seat)`

-- Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act?
-- c025: Chloe, the day before her 18th birthday.
#ASSERT `Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act` `as the young person` 20030314 20210313 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act` `as the young person` 20030314 20210313 EQUALS (`yes if` (`Am I a juvenile` 20030314 20210313))
-- c025: on her birthday.
#ASSERT `Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act` `as the young person` 20030314 20210314 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act` `as the young person` 20030314 20210314 EQUALS (`yes if` (`Am I a juvenile` 20030314 20210314))
#ASSERT `Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act` `as the adult` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act` `as the licensee or seller` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

